LC 349 — Intersection of Two Arrays
Pattern:Hashing

Logic:
Put elements of nums1 into a set.
Check which elements of nums2 are present.
Use another set so duplicates appear only once.

Algorithm:
Store nums1 in set
Check nums2
If found → add to answer

CODE:
class Solution {
public:
    vector<int> intersection(vector<int>& a, vector<int>& b) {
        unordered_set<int> s(a.begin(), a.end()), ans;

        for (int x : b)
            if (s.count(x))
                ans.insert(x);

        return vector<int>(ans.begin(), ans.end());
    }
};

EX:
nums1 = [1,2,2,1]
nums2 = [2,2]

nums1 set = {1,2}

2 found → add 2
2 already added → ignore

Answer = [2] ✅

Complexity:

Time: O(n + m)
Space: O(n)









